  "body": "Allow single-cut global swallowtails (keyhole cavities and tiny corner ears) to heal within `heal_tolerance`, and verify end-to-end with `sim::verify::wire`.\n\n## Context\n\nToday `ring::wire_ring` (`crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ring.rs`) rejects any `Region::offset_sharp` result that does not return `[one]` loop. When a `Punch` has a narrow-mouth keyhole notch (`< 2k` at the neck, `> 2k` inside), Clipper2 emits one outer cut loop plus an unreachable internal void loop. When a `Die` has a narrow corner ear pinched off by `k`, Clipper2 emits the main opening plus a tiny detached loop.\n\n## What this does\n\n- Add a bounded multi-loop selector for `heal_tolerance > 0.0` in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/ring.rs` (used by `wire_contour_ruled`):\n  - For `Punch`, keep the single outer loop (positive area) when any additional hole/void loops fall inside `heal_tolerance` under `laws::cover`.\n  - For `Die`, keep the loop that contains the stated `start` hole when any detached secondary ears fall inside `heal_tolerance` under `laws::cover`.\n  - Refuse total collapse (`[]`), a `start` hole outside every surviving loop, and any split into two main chambers that exceed `heal_tolerance`.\n- Add integration tests in `crates/app/tests/` running generation through `sim::verify::wire` (`kerf`, `threading`, and `slug` laws) to verify healed cuts never gouge or drop the wrong slug.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- A `Punch` keyhole or `Die` corner ear within `heal_tolerance` generates one closed loop, reports its uncut rest, and passes `sim::verify::wire`.\n- True bottleneck splits above `heal_tolerance` still trigger named refusals.\n\nPart of #2690\n",
